Chatwoot is an open-source, self-hosted customer support platform that
centralizes conversations across multiple channels into a single inbox.

It supports live chat via website widget, email, Facebook, Instagram,
Twitter/X, WhatsApp (Meta Cloud API and Twilio), Telegram, Line, SMS
(Twilio/Bandwidth), and a custom API channel.

Key features:
- Shared team inbox with assignment and auto-routing
- AI-assisted responses (Captain agent)
- Canned responses, labels, and conversation automation
- Multi-lingual support (30+ languages)
- Contact and CRM management with custom attributes
- Rich webhook and REST API
- Slack and Linear integrations
- Self-hosted, MIT-licensed — you own your data

Chatwoot requires PostgreSQL (>= 14) and Redis (>= 6.2) to operate.
Both must be configured before running the post-install setup steps.

WWW: https://www.chatwoot.com/
